/*
 * STEP 14B-34-H -- EXPLICIT AUDIO DEVICE CONFIGURATION (owner decision:
 * Option B of STEP 14B-34-G).
 *
 * The audio backend interface has accepted a device name end to end since
 * 14B-34-C/34-D: BounceAudioPlayerConfig.device_name flows through
 * bounce_audio_player_create() into the portable backend's open(), and the ALSA
 * backend passes it to snd_pcm_open(). Nothing in the tree ever POPULATED that
 * field, so the game always asked for the backend's own default, "default".
 *
 * This is the smallest mechanism that lets a caller name the device explicitly.
 * It is a command-line flag because that is the project's EXISTING startup
 * configuration mechanism: main() already parses startup options in a strcmp
 * chain and reports them through print_usage(). A new environment variable would
 * have meant a new constant plus a new accessor, which is a larger change, and an
 * environment variable is also less obviously explicit to a reader.
 *
 * WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
 *   - It does NOT probe. There is no candidate list and no enumeration.
 *   - It does NOT fall back. The named device is used or the player fails.
 *   - It does NOT silently substitute another device, and it does NOT turn a
 *     device failure into the Null backend. Null stays reachable only through the
 *     pre-existing explicit backend selection, and bounce_audio_player.c already
 *     enforces that: AUTO and ALSA both mean "want ALSA", and a failed open
 *     returns failure rather than degrading.
 *   - It does NOT change the default. With no flag, device_name stays NULL, which
 *     is byte-for-byte the behaviour that existed before this checkpoint.
 *
 * PORTABILITY. The value is an opaque string handed to the backend and never
 * interpreted here, so "plughw:1,0" is ALSA's namespace and a future WASAPI
 * backend would interpret the same field as an endpoint identifier. No
 * ALSA-specific semantics are added to the portable backend interface.
 *
 * The length is written out rather than using sizeof()-1 on a string literal so
 * the prefix compare and the parse cannot drift apart.
 */
#define BOUNCE_AUDIO_DEVICE_FLAG "--audio-device="
#define BOUNCE_AUDIO_DEVICE_FLAG_LENGTH 15u
/*
 * STEP SAVE-DIR -- the same shape as the audio flag, for the same reason: the prefix
 * compare and the parse cannot drift apart. The flag sets BOUNCE_SAVE_DIR, which
 * persistence.c resolves ahead of $XDG_DATA_HOME.
 */
#define BOUNCE_SAVE_DIR_FLAG "--save="
#define BOUNCE_SAVE_DIR_FLAG_LENGTH 7u
/* A high score no real path reaches, used to prove a file is this run's. */
#define BOUNCE_SAVE_PROBE_MARKER 424242
/* Distinct from the probe marker so a planted store can never equal a probed one. */
#define BOUNCE_SAVE_PLANT_MARKER 515151
